+---
+id: dl-002-availability-validates-its-query-like-quote-and-returns-sorted-ids
+type: decision-log
+title: "availability validates its query like quote and returns sorted ids"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+## Context
+
+The desk needs to list what can still be rented for a period, optionally for one kind.
+
+## Decision
+
+`availability(query)` applies the same period rules as `quote` and `book` (strict UTC-midnight format,
+end after start, half-open overlap, see dl-001) and throws on an invalid period or an unknown `kind`,
+rather than returning an empty list. The result is the ids sorted with the default string order, so it is
+deterministic and independent of registration order. An empty array means nothing is free.
+
+## Consequences
+
+A typo in a query surfaces as an error instead of looking like "nothing available". The overlap check is
+a single helper shared with `book`, so the two cannot drift apart.
